               Plasmodium falciparum was detected in 56/108 (51.8\%)
               individuals. Co-infections were also detected, with influenza
               A(H1N1)pdm09 virus in 16/56 (28.6\%) and severe acute respiratory
               syndrome coronavirus 2 in 10/56 (17.9\%) individuals. No novel
               pathogens were detected via metagenomics. Our findings suggest
               that the outbreak was primarily associated with a surge in
               malaria cases, with concurrent viral respiratory infections.
